<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="bc694784">&lt;p&gt;
    Identify on-going or planned initiatives in the organization and analyze whether they could have an impact on the
    project. This can be accomplished by conducting interviews or requesting corresponding data from the client. Consider
    integration strategies for the related initiatives.&amp;nbsp; This task may also identify initiatives that are duplicative
    or contradictory to the project, which will indicate the need to rationalize them or find other strategies to mitigate
    the corresponding risks to the project.&amp;nbsp; The results of the analysis should be discussed with the client to define
    appropriate actions.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="6f7cc8fe"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="fd6a76f6"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="9063181a"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="a2762094">To prevent adverse impact of other on-going client initiatives on the project. To leverage complementary initiatives that
could provide synergetic effect.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="79076d9"></attribute>
